/*
 * Implements validation for `await` expressions in Ymir.
 *
 * An `await` suspends the body of the async it appears in until the async value
 * it awaits completes, the thread of the future value it awaits finishes, or the
 * method poll of the class it awaits returns a value, the value it completes with
 * being the one of the await.
 * Without a value, it gives control back to the driver of the async.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::control::await_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/control/await_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-27
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
